-- title:
--   Integral n-th power adjustment of modular functions over ℚ̄
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be a finite-index subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$ containing $T = \begin{pmatrix}1&1\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and let $n$ be a positive natural number. Write $F_0 =$ [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) for the intermediate field of $\mathbb Q((q))$ over $\mathbb Q$ generated by the set of Laurent series of the shape `intSeriesC ℚ pf / intSeriesC ℚ pg`, where $k \in \mathbb Z$, where $f, g$ are modular forms of weight $k$ on the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}(2,\mathbb R)$, and where $pf, pg$ are power series over $\mathbb Z$ recording their integral $q$-expansions in the sense of `IsIntegralQExp`, subject to `intSeriesC ℚ pg ≠ 0`; and let $F =$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) F₀`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) be the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise images of $F_0$ under $\mathbb Q \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$. The assertion is that for every nonzero $f \in F$ there exist a nonzero $h \in F$ and a Laurent series $y$ over $A$ such that the Laurent series underlying $f h^n$ is the coefficientwise image of $y$ along the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$, and such that the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ along $A \to A/\mathfrak m_A$ is nonzero.
--
--   This is the Gauss-content normalisation for the function field of $X(\Gamma)$ read through $q$-expansions at the cusp $\infty$: modulo $n$-th powers, every nonzero modular function may be taken to have coefficients in a given valuation ring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with nonzero reduction. It is used in the construction of reduced root functions, entering [`ModularCurve.exists_reducedRootFunction_torsion_mem_finPts_iff_forall_dvd_ord_of_abelJacobiPin_tauFree_of_algEquiv`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_reducedRootFunction_torsion_mem_finPts_iff_forall_dvd_ord_of_abelJacobiPin_tauFree_of_algEquiv).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_mul_pow_coe_eq_coeffMap_and_coeffMap_residue_ne_zero_laurentBaseChange_qExpFunctionFieldC.lean

